                <pb facs="0251" n="1085" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1085"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112Sa/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-09T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.34 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>874. Department’s telegram No. 374, July 6. Minister for Foreign Affairs informed
                    me this morning that a delegation representing Norwegian shipowners will shortly
                    proceed to Berlin for the purpose of discussing with the German authorities the
                    question of safe conduct for Norwegian vessels. He stated that the main object
                    of the visit of the delegation to Berlin is to get a definite statement of
                    German desires in connection with these safe conducts, but that the delegation
                    would have no power to negotiate. He added that the delegation was more
                    particularly interested in insuring the safety of the passenger vessels <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bergensfjord</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stavangerfjord</hi>. Minister for Foreign Affairs also said that Sweden and
                    Denmark were sending similar delegates and that when the Norwegian delegation
                    returned from Berlin he hoped to obtain sufficiently clear information to enable
                    this Government to formulate a policy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
